<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Mr. Rousseau returns five weeks after the psychiatry consultation. He has had three sessions of cognitive behavioral therapy for psychosis and says the psychologist listens to him without calling him mad. He keeps a sleep diary and now rises at the same time each day; he sleeps about four and a half to five hours. He still holds the same beliefs about his former friends but has agreed with the psychologist to test one fear each week, and he has opened two letters he had set aside, which contained nothing he feared. He again declined aripiprazole today, saying he would rather see what the therapy does first. He met the urology surgeon three weeks ago, read the information on each option, and has chosen urethroplasty, which is booked in two weeks. He has used no sounds for seven weeks; his stream is thin but he has not been unable to pass urine. He has had no thoughts of suicide or of harming anyone. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Psychotherapy</td><td>Three CBT sessions; weekly behavioral tests of one fear</td></tr><tr><td>Sleep</td><td>Four and a half to five hours; fixed rising time</td></tr><tr><td>Medication decision</td><td>Aripiprazole declined again; offer remains open</td></tr><tr><td>Urology decision</td><td>Chose excision and primary anastomosis urethroplasty, booked in two weeks</td></tr><tr><td>Urethral rest</td><td>No sounds for seven weeks; no retention</td></tr><tr><td>Safety</td><td>No thoughts of suicide or of harming anyone</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

