    <title>Problems</title>
    <text><table><thead><tr><th>Problem</th><th>Clinical status</th><th>Verification</th><th>Code</th><th>Provenance</th></tr></thead><tbody>
  <tr ID="problem-1">
    <td>Fixed beliefs that former friends and colleagues are plotting to ruin him, with poor sleep, present for years and worse over the past year; cause not yet established; psychiatric and medical assessment under way</td><td>resolved</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>R46.5</td><td>S — Synthetic presenting concern at the index visit, superseded by the diagnosis at the psychiatry consultation; his documented beliefs of 1766 are echoed.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr ID="problem-2">
    <td>Weak urinary stream, straining, incomplete emptying (post-void residual 180 mL), and painful urination since childhood, treated for years by self-dilation with urethral sounds; cause not yet established; urethral imaging and endoscopy booked</td><td>resolved</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>R33.9</td><td>S — Synthetic presenting concern at the index visit, superseded by the urethrogram and cystoscopy diagnosis; his documented lifelong retention and self-treatment with bougies are echoed.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr ID="problem-3">
    <td>Delusional disorder, persecutory type (DSM-5-TR), of about nine years&apos; duration, with non-bizarre beliefs of a coordinated campaign against him; no hallucinations, disorganization, or mood episode; normal cognition; insomnia secondary to preoccupation; synthetic modern counterpart of his documented persecutory beliefs</td><td>active</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>F22</td><td>S — Synthetic modern diagnosis. His beliefs and conduct are documented (D); calling them a paranoid delusion is a retrospective interpretation (R), made difficult by the real persecution he suffered.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr ID="problem-4">
    <td>Bulbar urethral stricture, 1.5 cm, dense and ring-like (lumen about 8 French), idiopathic and probably congenital in origin, with decades of self-dilation; bladder trabeculation without hydronephrosis; kidney function normal; synthetic modern counterpart of his documented lifelong urinary retention</td><td>active</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>N35.812</td><td>S — Synthetic modern diagnosis. His lifelong retention is documented (D); its cause is disputed (R), and the autopsy found no urethral lesion (D), so this stricture is not presented as his historical diagnosis.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr ID="problem-5">
    <td>Right inguinal hernia, reducible and minimally symptomatic, likely aggravated by years of straining to pass urine</td><td>active</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>K40.90</td><td>S — Synthetic finding on examination; it echoes the documented rupture of 1758, whose site the source does not state.</td>
  </tr></tbody></table></text>

