<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.9" extension="2014-06-09"/>
    <code code="51847-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation + Plan note"/>
    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Delusional disorder, persecutory type (F22)</content>. Engaged in CBT for psychosis, with less distress and a little more flexibility about one belief; sleep still short. PHQ-9 7. He has again made an informed choice not to take an antipsychotic now, which is respected. Risk remains low. He has the capacity to consent to the operation: he understands the options, appreciates how they apply to him, weighs them, and states a consistent choice, and his beliefs do not concern the surgical team. [S]<list><item>Continue CBT for psychosis.</item><item>Aripiprazole remains available whenever he wants to try it.</item><item>Safety plan reviewed and unchanged; the 988 Suicide &amp; Crisis Lifeline confirmed.</item><item>Monthly PHQ-9 to be done at his CBT sessions, after the February check was missed.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Bulbar urethral stricture before urethroplasty (N35.812)</content>. Seven weeks of urethral rest without retention; residual 210 mL. Creatinine 1.04 mg/dL and hemoglobin 14.4 g/dL; urinalysis without infection, and the urology team&apos;s urine culture showed no growth, so he is fit for surgery. [S]<list><item>Excision and primary anastomosis bulbar urethroplasty in two weeks, his choice; consent signed with the urology team.</item><item>Catheter for about three weeks, with a urethrogram around the catheter before it is removed.</item><item>Acetaminophen for pain afterwards rather than opioids, which can cause constipation and retention.</item><item>Continue urethral rest; come in the same day if he cannot pass urine.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Protocol monitoring: items the monitoring protocol calls for at this visit. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Domain</th><th>Measure</th><th>Interval</th><th>Status</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Suicide and violence risk review (C-SSRS Since Last Visit, PHQ-9 item 9, thoughts of harming others, plans to confront anyone, access to weapons) and the safety plan</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>No thoughts of suicide or of harming anyone; no plan to confront anyone; no weapons; PHQ-9 item 9 scored 0; safety plan reviewed</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>PHQ-9 for depressive symptoms</td><td>Baseline, then at least monthly while symptoms are being treated</td><td>Completed today</td><td>7, down from 8</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Monthly PHQ-9 between the first visit and today</td><td>At least monthly</td><td>Deferred</td><td>Missed: the check due in mid-February was not done because there was no visit between the second visit and today. Today&apos;s score is lower, and no worsening of mood was reported to the psychologist, so no harm is judged to have resulted. Corrective action: the psychologist will give the PHQ-9 at each CBT session</td></tr><tr><td>Referral</td><td>Cognitive behavioral therapy for psychosis</td><td>About 16 sessions</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Three sessions so far; engaged</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>Antipsychotic offered again</td><td>When declined, offered again at later visits</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Declined again; his reasons recorded; offer kept open</td></tr><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>Metabolic baseline and AIMS before an antipsychotic</td><td>Before starting</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>No antipsychotic started</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>IPSS</td><td>At diagnosis, before surgery, and after treatment</td><td>Completed today</td><td>22, severe</td></tr><tr><td>Imaging</td><td>Post-void residual during urethral rest</td><td>Before surgery and with any change in voiding</td><td>Completed today</td><td>210 mL; no retention</td></tr><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>Creatinine, eGFR, potassium, hemoglobin, and urinalysis before surgery</td><td>Before urethroplasty</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Creatinine 1.04 mg/dL, eGFR 85, potassium 4.3 mmol/L, hemoglobin 14.4 g/dL, u